{"n": 1, "system_tail": "location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>synth-manage-checks</name>\n    <description>Creates, updates, exports, and deletes Synthetic Monitoring checks from YAML definitions via gcx. Use when the user wants to create, update, pull, push, or delete Synthetic Monitoring checks. Trigger on phrases like &quot;create a check&quot;, &quot;add a synthetic check&quot;, &quot;update check&quot;, &quot;pull my SM checks&quot;, &quot;push checks&quot;, &quot;delete check&quot;, or when the user provides a target URL/hostname/domain for monitoring. For check status overview use synth-check-status. For investigating failing checks use synth-investigate-check.</description>\n    <location>/Users/danielbooth/.agents/skills/synth-manage-checks/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n</available_skills>\n</skills>\n\n<cwd>\n/Users/danielbooth/projects/work/danielboothcloud/pi-aio/test/.pigcheck/rc-work/rpc-hypa\n</cwd>", "last": {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[DEFAULT MODE ACTIVE]\n- edit, write, and apply_patch tools require per-call user approval (files outside the working directory get a separate outside-directory approval)\n- bash and hypa_shell commands outside the simple read-only allowlist require per-call user approval\n- Python/Node scripts, compound commands, and execution-capable wrappers require approval too; never use them to bypass edit/write approval\n- simple read-only shell commands and reads (read/grep/find/ls) pass through without prompting\nWhen a cheap check (test, command, log) would answer a question, run it rather than speculating."}]}}
